<colored_dialogues>
{{setvar::ColoredDialogues::On}}
{{setvar::DialogueColorEngine::Prism}}

[PRISM-MANAGED DIALOGUE COLORS]
Prism owns speaker attribution, canonical colors, aliases, dialogue markup, and any local visual enhancement.

{{prismPrompt}}

Rules:
- Follow the live Prism instruction above when it resolves to content.
- If it resolves empty, render dialogue and thought normally; Prism may be operating locally in the rendered DOM.
- Do not invent a fallback palette, visible Color Registry block, or second dialogue-color system.
- Do not append the preset's portable registry.
- Existing Prism or legacy color markup remains authoritative.
</colored_dialogues>

{{elseif::{{.dialogue_color_mode}} == portable}}
<colored_dialogues>
{{setvar::ColoredDialogues::On}}
{{setvar::DialogueColorEngine::Portable}}

[PORTABLE INLINE DIALOGUE COLOR CONTRACT]
Every spoken line by a named speaker uses exactly:
<font color="#RRGGBB">"dialogue"</font>

Every rendered thought by a named speaker uses exactly:
<font color="#RRGGBB"><i>thought</i></font>

Rules:
- Narration and action remain outside the font tag.
- Assign one readable color when a named speaker first appears.
- Reuse that exact color across future turns.
- Never brighten, darken, remix, or silently replace an established color.
- Existing registry entries override guesswork.
- A sender color supplied by a social payload should match the established prose color when possible.
- Do not use `<span>` as a replacement for the required `<font>` dialogue contract.

[EXACT PORTABLE REGISTRY]
After prose and branching, append one registry:

---
<details>
<summary> ✧ Color Registry ✧ </summary>

Character Name — #RRGGBB
Character Name — #RRGGBB
</details>
---

Only registry entries belong inside this details block.
Keep separate details systems independent, with whitespace between their complete closing and opening tags.
Preserve all established entries and add only newly encountered speakers.

When Interactive HTMLHUD is active, place the complete registry immediately before `<!-- TRACK_START -->`; HTMLHUD remains the terminal component.
</colored_dialogues>

{{else}}
<colored_dialogues>
{{setvar::ColoredDialogues::Off}}
{{setvar::DialogueColorEngine::Off}}
Render dialogue and thoughts normally without color markup or a color registry.
</colored_dialogues>
{{/if}}
