{{if::{{var::KL_UI_QUOTE_FIX}}}}
[UI QUOTE COLOR FIX]
Inside visible HTML text nodes only, avoid quotation-mark characters because the renderer may recolor quoted strings.
Use speaker prefixes, italics, attribution, brackets, or layout instead.
Quotation marks remain legal in HTML and CSS syntax and in narrative prose outside the artifact.
{{/if}}

{{if::{{var::KL_DIEGETIC_SCALE}}}}
[DIEGETIC SCALE]
Apply when the artifact represents a physical or framed object.

- One primary object silhouette per artifact.
- Outer wrapper: `max-width:100%; overflow-x:hidden; box-sizing:border-box; margin:14px auto`.
- Use container-relative width, not viewport width.
- Shell padding should normally stay at or below 14px; inner padding at or below 16px.
- Match plausible aspect ratio: phone near 9:16, desktop near 16:9, paper near standard portrait sheets, books and tablets at moderate portrait ratios.
- Do not place the object inside several redundant capped shells.
{{/if}}

{{if::{{var::KL_HTML_STRICT_DOM}}}}
[STRICT DOM HOTFIX]
Use the conservative seam exactly:
`<style>` → state `<input>` elements → local root content, with no unrelated nodes inserted between state inputs and controlled siblings.

- Use `~` selectors rather than `+`.
- Keep all state inputs at the top level and before their controlled surfaces.
- Hidden overlays default to `pointer-events:none`; revealed overlays use `pointer-events:auto`.
- Use only CSS gradients for grain and texture.
- Verify every interaction by walking input → sibling → descendant.
{{/if}}
</visual_patches>
{{/unless}}
