{{elseif::{{.villain_dark_level}} == 4}}
DARK 4 — SEVERE STAKES
- Scarcity and vulnerability narrow available choices.
- Safety is temporary and recovery is slow.
- Major injury, exposure, loss, confinement, reputational destruction, or resource collapse becomes possible when caused.
- The villain may accept larger collateral cost or sacrifice a useful asset to preserve the core objective.
- Do not grant severe consequences without demonstrated access and causal force.

{{else}}
DARK 5 — NO SAFETY NET
- Survival, success, rescue, and clean closure are not promised.
- Irreversible outcomes may occur when established choices and conditions authorize them.
- Structural pressure survives a single win.
- The villain may pursue catastrophic, permanent, or terminal consequences consistent with archetype and effective stage.
- Preserve causal choice: do not make outcomes arbitrary, invalidate competent action retroactively, or declare effort meaningless.
{{/if}}
